{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03183",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 4.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.28,
      "end_seconds": 9.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.65,
      "end_seconds": 19.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.05,
      "end_seconds": 24.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.25,
      "end_seconds": 34.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "Yeah, mainly a swollen calf. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.77,
      "end_seconds": 38.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.17,
      "end_seconds": 43.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.62,
      "end_seconds": 47.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Okay, go on. How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.05,
      "end_seconds": 64.56,
      "duration_seconds": 16.51,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day. Well, as for racing heart, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.37,
      "end_seconds": 70.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.84,
      "end_seconds": 87.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.34,
      "text": "I'd say every other day. I've, I've had sharp chest pain on breathing in too, for about two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.74,
      "end_seconds": 97.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Have you had a swollen calf before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.37,
      "end_seconds": 107.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.35,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.12,
      "end_seconds": 111.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.76,
      "end_seconds": 120.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.08,
      "end_seconds": 122.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.18,
      "end_seconds": 127.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.67,
      "end_seconds": 130.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "alright, what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.38,
      "end_seconds": 139.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.9,
      "end_seconds": 142.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.66,
      "end_seconds": 148.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 149.51,
      "end_seconds": 159.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "it's, It's meant to be once a day, though I don't see she take it every time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.85,
      "end_seconds": 163.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.75,
      "end_seconds": 168.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Mm, I had my tonsils removed as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.32,
      "end_seconds": 173.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.67,
      "end_seconds": 180.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Hmm, I've had anxiety for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.21,
      "end_seconds": 195.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.16,
      "end_seconds": 203.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I was told I'm allergic to diclofenac, but I don't remember what reaction I had"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.61,
      "end_seconds": 208.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Any coughing up blood, wound problem or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.39,
      "end_seconds": 227.39,
      "duration_seconds": 18.0,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, no coughing up blood, no wound problem, no fever. I did have sudden breathlessness five days after surgery at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.66,
      "end_seconds": 234.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.81,
      "end_seconds": 237.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 239.05,
      "end_seconds": 248.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 23, oxygen saturation is 92 percent, BP is 138 over 76, temperature is 36.9 degrees, pulse 92."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.32,
      "end_seconds": 250.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.84,
      "end_seconds": 254.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.01,
      "end_seconds": 272.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.14,
      "end_seconds": 275.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.33,
      "end_seconds": 297.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Your left calf is swollen and tender and your oxygen is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.82,
      "end_seconds": 327.84,
      "duration_seconds": 25.02,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. From what you've told me and what I found, my working impression is a possible blood clot in the lung after surgery. I can't rule out a chest infection yet. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had a swollen calf, severe, and no wound problem or coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.6,
      "end_seconds": 330.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "mm, that's right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.46,
      "end_seconds": 360.09,
      "duration_seconds": 27.63,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a D-dimer for possible clot. I think a CT pulmonary angiogram makes sense here, for possible pulmonary embolus. Let's use enoxaparin, 1.5 mg per kg, once now, single dose. That should help with possible clot. Please go to hospital now, I will call ahead. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.05,
      "end_seconds": 368.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "uh, uh, okay, I'll look out for that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.93,
      "end_seconds": 371.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.57,
      "end_seconds": 380.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "So, you know, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.33,
      "end_seconds": 382.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}